0..60 Comment "//! `ring-base` defines the mock ring protocols and entries."
61..64 Comment "//!"
65..144 Comment "//! Each submission owes one completion. The io_uring(7) manual states \"exactly"
145..225 Comment "//! one matching CQE for every SQE\". A read buffer moves into its submission and"
226..305 Comment "//! returns with its completion, because the kernel owns it while the operation"
306..386 Comment "//! is in flight [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]. The pathological twins refuse a"
387..457 Comment "//! completion left pending and a buffer reused before its completion."
458..461 Comment "//!"
462..541 Comment "//! The checker gives the submitter a pending completion after it sends `read`."
542..614 Comment "//! The imported declarations give every completion source one protocol."
615..618 Comment "//!"
619..682 Comment "//! - see: corpus/pathological/completion/pending-dropped.gandr"
683..745 Comment "//! - see: corpus/pathological/completion/buffer-touched.gandr"
746..789 Comment "//! - cites: [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]"
790..793 Comment "//!"
794..893 Comment "//! [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]: https://without.boats/blog/io-uring/ \"boats, Notes on io-uring\""
895..967 Comment "/// A ring: its entries sealed behind the interface, the protocol of one"
968..1045 Comment "/// submission as the kernel serves it, the buffer and the pending completion"
1046..1118 Comment "/// on the submitter\'s side, the protocols that take a buffer, a pending"
1119..1196 Comment "/// completion or a target\'s pending completion over a session, and one entry"
1197..1214 Comment "/// of each kind."
